{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107045","id":2560431368,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6YnRUI","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107045","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107045.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107045.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107045","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107045/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107045/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107045/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/46b88dcbda34527cd5a132a2c5cba889eb61f3c8","number":107045,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rename internal fields and variables in `AHashMap`, `HashMap` and `HashSet`","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`AHashMap`, `HashMap` and `HashSet` have inconsistent field and variable names - not only between themselves, but also internally, and across the codebase.\r\nWhen I personally tried to understand the code, this threw me off many times, and made the classes extremely hard to understand and compare.\r\n\r\nI've renamed variables to be consistent. This should help these classes be more maintainable.\r\n\r\n## Change List\r\n\r\n**HashMapData name:** `AHashMap` uses (globally declared) `HashMapData` to store `hash` and `element_idx`. However, the name makes it sounds like it stores data.\r\n**Solution:** I've renamed the field to `AHashMap::Metadata`. This is consistent with naming terminology of hash maps in other libraries.\r\n\r\n**`AHashMap::Metadata` is a struct of a union of a struct or `uint64_t`:** This is very confusing. \r\n**Solution:** I've changed `Metadata` to be a `struct`, and whenever both elements are assigned at once, a `Metadata` instance is used, instead of assigning `.data` union. I tested performance (`get`, `get missing`, `insert`, `insert existing`, `erase`), and found no regressions (if anything, it's 1-2% faster now).\r\n\r\n**Indexes are inconsistently named:** Indexes are named `pos`, `index`, `idx`, `kpos`, `hpos`, among others. Further, in `AHashMap` and `HashSet`, `pos` may refer to either key or hash index inconsistently, even within the same function. This makes it extremely difficult to know at a glance which kind of index you're looking at.\r\n**Solution:** `HashMap` has only one kind of index. All indices are called `idx`. `AHashMap` has elements and metadata, so it now uses `metadata_idx` and `element_idx`. `HashSet` has hashes and keys, so it now uses `hash_idx` and `key_idx`. `capacity_idx` is now consistently named `capacity_idx`.\r\n\r\n**Fields are indistinguishable from local variables:** For example, `AHashMap` has local `capacity` and the field `capacity`. \r\n**Solution:** Private fields are prefixed with underscore `_` to mark them as such.\r\n\r\n**capacity is indistinguishable from capacity mask:** `AHashMap` has field `capacity`, but it's actually `capacity - 1`.\r\n**Solution:** I've renamed the field to `_capacity_mask`.\r\n\r\n**num_elements is inconsistent with `size` of other containers:** Other collections like `Array` use `size()` to refer to the number of elements in the collection. The public APIs of hash maps also use `size()`, but the internal field is called `num_elements`.\r\n**Solution:** `num_elements` is renamed to `size` for consistency.\r\n\r\nThere are other, smaller changes to pull everything together, but I think this covers the big ones.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"h